WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
01  NITROGEN PURGE
Nitrogen flows through the fuel preheater, cracker and anode before fuel admission.

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:20.000
02  CONTROLLED COLD START
External electric heating raises the thermal inventories. Physical time is accelerated.

3
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:30.000
03  AMMONIA CRACKING / CURRENT RAMP
Current is admitted after the model temperature and conversion checks.

4
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:40.000
04  HEAT-INTEGRATED GENERATION
Separate anode and cathode exhaust streams supply the tail-gas oxidizer and heat cascade.

5
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:50.000
05  ISLANDED LOAD TRANSITIONS
Battery power buffers the load increase and reduction while SOFC current ramps.

6
00:00:50.000 --> 00:01:00.000
06  METERED SOC RESTORATION
SOC returns to 0.65 through the battery power port. External electricity remains counted.

7
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:10.000
07  FUEL / CURRENT SHUTDOWN
Fuel and current decrease; recovery is bypassed and nitrogen purge resumes.

8
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:30.000
08  CONTROLLED COOLDOWN
Cathode air assists cooling; nitrogen purge continues. Below 80 C is a model endpoint.
